  [PASS] no rung on disk is within 3 sigma of the framework's own prediction for that rung  [CAN FAIL -- and it FAILS AGAINST THE FRAMEWORK, which is the result]   (open clusters (1 pc, 1e3 Msun): 5.4 sigma; vertical force (1 kpc, 1e10 Msun): 11.3 sigma)
  [PASS] the vertical-force rung's measured boost is BELOW its own prediction, i.e. the disc is boosted LESS than the kernel requires  [CAN FAIL]   (measured 1.123 +- 0.028 (Bovy & Rix) or 1.230 +- 0.100 (McMillan) vs predicted 1.444)
  BOTH WAYS, and it matters: on the McMillan normalisation the vertical-force rung is 2.1 sigma from
  the framework and 2.3 sigma from Newton -- that rung's 10% inter-measurement disagreement is larger
  than the whole signal, so it is not decisive either.  Only the Bovy & Rix normalisation makes it look sharp.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
B2.  THE EQUALITY TEST the candidate actually proposes: is ONE B consistent with the rungs?
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  best single B across the 2 MEASURED rungs: 1.102 +- 0.028   chi2 = 14.2 / 1 dof  (p = 0.000834 for 1 dof)
     open clusters (1 pc, 1e3 Msun)                 0.589 +- 0.139   (-3.7 sigma from the common value)
     vertical force (1 kpc, 1e10 Msun)              1.123 +- 0.028   (+0.8 sigma from the common value)
  [PASS] the two measured rungs are NOT consistent with a single shared B, so the cross-class equality is refuted by the data as well as by the theory  [CAN FAIL]   (chi2/dof = 14.2 on 2 rungs)
  AND NOTE WHAT THAT CHI-SQUARED IS NOT.  With only two measured rungs (open clusters and the vertical
  force) a 'cross-class law spanning fifteen decades of mass' has TWO points, both inside 1 kpc of the Sun,
  and their separation (0.534) is dominated by systematics neither script can close.

  SO THE CHI-SQUARED MUST BE REDONE WITH SYSTEMATICS, and doing so REVERSES it -- reported because it goes
  against the kill, not for it.  The open-cluster rung's B swings 0.59 -> 1.06 on one modelling choice (a
  free vs zero non-virial floor) and 0.59 -> 1.02 on another (whether M_phot carries the catalogue's IMF
  extrapolation).  The vertical-force rung swings 1.123 -> 1.230 between two published measurements of the
  same quantity.  Carrying those as systematics:
     open clusters   B = 0.82 +- 0.25 (stat + the two modelling swings, half-range)
     vertical force  B = 1.18 +- 0.09 (stat + the Bovy-Rix / McMillan disagreement)
     -> common B = 1.139, chi2 = 1.84 / 1 dof: the two rungs ARE mutually consistent once
        systematics are carried, and the common value is 1.6 sigma from Newton's 1.000 and 2.4 sigma from the law's 1.341.
  [PASS] with systematics carried, the equality is NOT refuted by the data -- so the honest statement is that the DATA cannot test the cross-class claim, and only the THEORY refutes it  [CAN FAIL]   (chi2 = 1.84/1 dof with systematics vs 14.2/1 without)
  The systematics-inclusive common value 1.139 sits BETWEEN Newton's 1.000 and the law's 1.341 and
  is consistent with both.  That is the whole measurement status of candidate 1 today.

